IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`

-- ccc7-s187-packet.l4 -- sections 187 (the sealed packet: confidentiality of the application documents and the accused's access to them), 189 (notice of intention to produce intercepted evidence; privilege)
-- and 190 (further particulars) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI. Section 189(1) to (4) is shown repealed in this text.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
-- What these sections mean to the person in the seat: the documents on which an authorization about them was given are sealed, and the accused can ask the trial judge to open them (section 187(1.4)),
-- gets an edited copy (187(4)-(5)) and can ask for the deleted parts (187(7)); the Crown must give reasonable notice, with a transcript or particulars, before using intercepted contents (189(5));
-- privileged information stays privileged (189(6)); and the judge may order further particulars (190).
-- A bar is named as the bar (JUST TRUE = it applies). A "may ... where" grant answers JUST FALSE when its "where" fails (the guide's ruling (b), listed for a lawyer: F11).

§ `Section 187 -- Manner in which application to be kept secret`

-- 187(1): "All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part are confidential and, subject to subsection (1.1), shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge to whom the application is made immediately on
-- determination of the application, and that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with
-- subsections (1.2) to (1.5)."
-- src:3909 | Manner in which application to be kept secret
-- src:3910 | 187 (1) All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part are confidential and, subject to subsection (1.1), shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge to whom the application is made immediately on determination of the application, and that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5).
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1) (src:3909-3910)
GIVEN `the document relates to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1) the document is confidential` MEANS
    IF `the document relates to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part"

-- 187(1.1): "An authorization given under this Part need not be placed in the packet except if, under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge, in which case that judge must place it in the packet and the copy
-- remains with the applicant." The function says the authorization need not be placed (JUST TRUE); the "except if" is JUST FALSE.
-- src:3911 | Exception
-- src:3912 | (1.1) An authorization given under this Part need not be placed in the packet except if, under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge, in which case that judge must place it in the packet and the copy remains with the applicant.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1.1) (src:3911-3912)
GIVEN `it is an authorization given under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1.1) the authorization need not be placed in the packet` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an authorization given under this Part`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An authorization given under this Part"
        IF `under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except if, under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3911 | Exception
-- src:3912 | (1.1) An authorization given under this Part need not be placed in the packet except if, under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge, in which case that judge must place it in the packet and the copy remains with the applicant.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1.1) (src:3911-3912)
GIVEN `under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1.1) the judge must place the original authorization in the packet and the copy remains with the applicant` MEANS
    IF `under subsection 184.3(8), the original authorization is in the hands of the judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in which case that judge must place it in the packet and the copy remains with the applicant"

-- 187(1): the documents "shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge ..." subject to (1.1): JUST TRUE = must be placed; JUST FALSE where (1.1) says the authorization need not be.
-- src:3909 | Manner in which application to be kept secret
-- src:3910 | 187 (1) All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part are confidential and, subject to subsection (1.1), shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge to whom the application is made immediately on determination of the application, and that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5).
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1) (src:3909-3910)
GIVEN `the document relates to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 187(1.1) the authorization need not be placed in the packet` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1) the document must be placed in a packet and sealed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the document relates to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part"
        IF `s 187(1.1) the authorization need not be placed in the packet` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to subsection (1.1), shall be placed in a packet"
        IF `s 187(1.1) the authorization need not be placed in the packet` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (1.1) excuses the document is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The packet "shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize".
-- src:3909 | Manner in which application to be kept secret
-- src:3910 | 187 (1) All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part are confidential and, subject to subsection (1.1), shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge to whom the application is made immediately on determination of the application, and that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5).
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1) (src:3909-3910)
GIVEN `the packet is kept in the custody of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is kept in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1) the packet is kept as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the packet is kept in the custody of the court` AND `it is kept in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize"

-- ... "and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5)". Named for the bar: JUST TRUE = the dealing is barred.
DECLARE `s 187(1) dealing with the packet` IS ONE OF
    `s 187(1) opening it to deal with an application for a further authorization or a renewal, under subsection (1.2)`
    `s 187(1) opening it on an order of a judge, under subsection (1.3)`
    `s 187(1) opening it on an order of the trial judge, under subsection (1.4)`
    `s 187(1) destroying its contents on an order, under subsection (1.5)`
    `s 187(1) any other dealing with it`

-- src:3909 | Manner in which application to be kept secret
-- src:3910 | 187 (1) All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part are confidential and, subject to subsection (1.1), shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge to whom the application is made immediately on determination of the application, and that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5).
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1) (src:3909-3910)
GIVEN dealing IS A `s 187(1) dealing with the packet`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1) the packet shall not be dealt with in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER dealing
    WHEN `s 187(1) opening it to deal with an application for a further authorization or a renewal, under subsection (1.2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5)"
    WHEN `s 187(1) opening it on an order of a judge, under subsection (1.3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5)"
    WHEN `s 187(1) opening it on an order of the trial judge, under subsection (1.4)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5)"
    WHEN `s 187(1) destroying its contents on an order, under subsection (1.5)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5)"
    WHEN `s 187(1) any other dealing with it` THEN JUST TRUE

-- The sealing duty as a regulative rule: "shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge ... immediately on determination of the application": no number of days is stated, so no WITHIN.
DECLARE `s 187(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 187(1) places the documents in a packet and seals it`

-- src:3909 | Manner in which application to be kept secret
-- src:3910 | 187 (1) All documents relating to an application made pursuant to any provision of this Part are confidential and, subject to subsection (1.1), shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge to whom the application is made immediately on determination of the application, and that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with subsections (1.2) to (1.5).
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1) (src:3909-3910)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 183 party under Part VI` `s 187(1) act`
`s 187(1) the duty to seal the packet as a rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 183 a judge`
    MUST `s 187(1) places the documents in a packet and seals it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 183 a judge` BECAUSE "s 187(1): the documents were not placed in a packet and sealed immediately on determination of the application"

-- 187(1.2): "The sealed packet may be opened and its contents removed for the purpose of dealing with an application for a further authorization or with an application for renewal of an authorization."
-- src:3913 | Opening for further applications
-- src:3914 | (1.2) The sealed packet may be opened and its contents removed for the purpose of dealing with an application for a further authorization or with an application for renewal of an authorization.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1.2) (src:3913-3914)
GIVEN `the purpose is dealing with an application for a further authorization or with an application for renewal of an authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1.2) the sealed packet may be opened and its contents removed` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is dealing with an application for a further authorization or with an application for renewal of an authorization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of dealing with an application for a further authorization or with an application for renewal of an authorization"

-- 187(1.3): "A provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 may order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed for the purpose of copying and examining the documents contained in the packet."
-- src:3915 | Opening on order of judge
-- src:3916 | (1.3) A provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 may order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed for the purpose of copying and examining the documents contained in the packet.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1.3) (src:3915-3916)
GIVEN `the person is a provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is copying and examining the documents contained in the packet` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1.3) the judge may order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed` MEANS
    IF `the person is a provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` AND `the purpose is copying and examining the documents contained in the packet`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of copying and examining the documents contained in the packet"

-- 187(1.4): "A judge or provincial court judge before whom a trial is to be held and who has jurisdiction in the province in which an authorization was given may order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed for the purpose of copying
-- and examining the documents contained in the packet if (a) any matter relevant to the authorization or any evidence obtained pursuant to the authorization is in issue in the trial; and (b) the accused applies for such an order for the purpose of consulting
-- the documents to prepare for trial." The accused's way to the papers. A grant with an "if" gate: NOTHING when the gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12, F8).
-- src:3917 | Opening on order of trial judge
-- src:3918 | (1.4) A judge or provincial court judge before whom a trial is to be held and who has jurisdiction in the province in which an authorization was given may order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed for the purpose of copying and examining the documents contained in the packet if
-- src:3919 | (a) any matter relevant to the authorization or any evidence obtained pursuant to the authorization is in issue in the trial; and
-- src:3920 | (b) the accused applies for such an order for the purpose of consulting the documents to prepare for trial.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1.4) (src:3917-3920)
GIVEN `the person is a judge or provincial court judge before whom a trial is to be held and who has jurisdiction in the province in which an authorization was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any matter relevant to the authorization or any evidence obtained pursuant to the authorization is in issue in the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused applies for such an order for the purpose of consulting the documents to prepare for trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1.4) the trial judge may order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge or provincial court judge before whom a trial is to be held and who has jurisdiction in the province in which an authorization was given`
       AND `any matter relevant to the authorization or any evidence obtained pursuant to the authorization is in issue in the trial`
       AND `the accused applies for such an order for the purpose of consulting the documents to prepare for trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if (a) any matter relevant to the authorization or any evidence obtained pursuant to the authorization is in issue in the trial; and (b) the accused applies for such an order"

-- 187(1.5): "Where a sealed packet is opened, its contents shall not be destroyed except pursuant to an order of a judge of the same court as the judge who gave the authorization." Named for the bar: JUST TRUE = the contents shall not be destroyed.
-- src:3921 | Order for destruction of documents
-- src:3922 | (1.5) Where a sealed packet is opened, its contents shall not be destroyed except pursuant to an order of a judge of the same court as the judge who gave the authorization.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(1.5) (src:3921-3922)
GIVEN `a sealed packet has been opened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the destruction is pursuant to an order of a judge of the same court as the judge who gave the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(1.5) the contents shall not be destroyed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a sealed packet has been opened`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a sealed packet is opened"
        IF `the destruction is pursuant to an order of a judge of the same court as the judge who gave the authorization`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except pursuant to an order of a judge of the same court as the judge who gave the authorization"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 187(2): "An order under subsection (1.2), (1.3), (1.4) or (1.5) made with respect to documents relating to an application made pursuant to section 185 or subsection 186(6) or 196(2) may only be made after the Attorney General or the Minister of
-- Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness by whom or on whose authority the application for the authorization to which the order relates was made has been given an opportunity to be heard." "may only be made after": JUST FALSE when not yet heard.
