        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be made after the Attorney General has been given an opportunity to be heard"

-- 187(4): "Where a prosecution has been commenced and an accused applies for an order for the copying and examination of documents pursuant to subsection (1.3) or (1.4), the judge shall not, notwithstanding those subsections, provide any copy of any document
-- to the accused until the prosecutor has deleted any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest, including any part that the prosecutor believes could (a) compromise the identity of any
-- confidential informant; (b) compromise the nature and extent of ongoing investigations; (c) endanger persons engaged in particular intelligence-gathering techniques and thereby prejudice future investigations in which similar techniques would be used;
-- or (d) prejudice the interests of innocent persons." Named for the bar: JUST TRUE before the prosecutor's deletion, JUST FALSE after it ("until": ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)); JUST FALSE where the "Where" fails.
-- src:3927 | Editing of copies
-- src:3928 | (4) Where a prosecution has been commenced and an accused applies for an order for the copying and examination of documents pursuant to subsection (1.3) or (1.4), the judge shall not, notwithstanding those subsections, provide any copy of any document to the accused until the prosecutor has deleted any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest, including any part that the prosecutor believes could
-- src:3929 | (a) compromise the identity of any confidential informant;
-- src:3930 | (b) compromise the nature and extent of ongoing investigations;
-- src:3931 | (c) endanger persons engaged in particular intelligence-gathering techniques and thereby prejudice future investigations in which similar techniques would be used; or
-- src:3932 | (d) prejudice the interests of innocent persons.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(4) (src:3927-3932)
GIVEN `a prosecution has been commenced and an accused applies for an order for the copying and examination of documents pursuant to subsection (1.3) or (1.4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has deleted any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(4) the judge shall not yet provide a copy of the document to the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a prosecution has been commenced and an accused applies for an order for the copying and examination of documents pursuant to subsection (1.3) or (1.4)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a prosecution has been commenced and an accused applies for an order for the copying and examination of documents pursuant to subsection (1.3) or (1.4)"
        IF `the prosecutor has deleted any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the prosecutor has deleted any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The parts the prosecutor deletes: "any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest, including any part that the prosecutor believes could (a) ... (d)". An "including" list: open.
DECLARE `s 187(4) part of the copy` IS ONE OF
    `s 187(4) a part that could compromise the identity of any confidential informant`
    `s 187(4) a part that could compromise the nature and extent of ongoing investigations`
    `s 187(4) a part that could endanger persons engaged in particular intelligence-gathering techniques and thereby prejudice future investigations in which similar techniques would be used`
    `s 187(4) a part that could prejudice the interests of innocent persons`
    `s 187(4) another part that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest`
    `s 187(4) a part that the prosecutor does not believe would be prejudicial to the public interest`

-- src:3927 | Editing of copies
-- src:3928 | (4) Where a prosecution has been commenced and an accused applies for an order for the copying and examination of documents pursuant to subsection (1.3) or (1.4), the judge shall not, notwithstanding those subsections, provide any copy of any document to the accused until the prosecutor has deleted any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest, including any part that the prosecutor believes could
-- src:3929 | (a) compromise the identity of any confidential informant;
-- src:3930 | (b) compromise the nature and extent of ongoing investigations;
-- src:3931 | (c) endanger persons engaged in particular intelligence-gathering techniques and thereby prejudice future investigations in which similar techniques would be used; or
-- src:3932 | (d) prejudice the interests of innocent persons.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(4) (src:3927-3932)
GIVEN part IS A `s 187(4) part of the copy`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(4) the prosecutor’s deletion covers the part` MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `s 187(4) a part that could compromise the identity of any confidential informant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 187(4) a part that could compromise the nature and extent of ongoing investigations` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 187(4) a part that could endanger persons engaged in particular intelligence-gathering techniques and thereby prejudice future investigations in which similar techniques would be used` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 187(4) a part that could prejudice the interests of innocent persons` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 187(4) another part that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 187(4) a part that the prosecutor does not believe would be prejudicial to the public interest` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any part of the copy of the document that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest"

-- 187(5): "After the prosecutor has deleted the parts of the copy of the document to be given to the accused under subsection (4), the accused shall be provided with an edited copy of the document." The text names no one who provides it
-- (fork F13): only the decision function is encoded, with no regulative rule, so that no actor is invented. A duty whose "After" is unmet is JUST FALSE (F9).
-- src:3933 | Accused to be provided with copies
-- src:3934 | (5) After the prosecutor has deleted the parts of the copy of the document to be given to the accused under subsection (4), the accused shall be provided with an edited copy of the document.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(5) (src:3933-3934)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has deleted the parts of the copy of the document to be given to the accused under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(5) the accused is to be provided with an edited copy of the document` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor has deleted the parts of the copy of the document to be given to the accused under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After the prosecutor has deleted the parts of the copy of the document to be given to the accused under subsection (4), the accused shall be provided with an edited copy of the document"

-- 187(6): "After the accused has received an edited copy of a document, the prosecutor shall keep a copy of the original document, and an edited copy of the document and the original document shall be returned to the packet and the packet resealed."
