`s 187(6) the prosecutor is bound to keep a copy of the original document` MEANS
    IF `the accused has received an edited copy of a document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After the accused has received an edited copy of a document, the prosecutor shall keep a copy of the original document"

DECLARE `s 187(6) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 187(6) keeps a copy of the original document`

-- src:3935 | Original documents to be returned
-- src:3936 | (6) After the accused has received an edited copy of a document, the prosecutor shall keep a copy of the original document, and an edited copy of the document and the original document shall be returned to the packet and the packet resealed.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(6) (src:3935-3936)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 183 party under Part VI` `s 187(6) act`
`s 187(6) the duty to keep a copy of the original document as a rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 183 the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 187(6) keeps a copy of the original document`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 183 the prosecutor` BECAUSE "s 187(6): the prosecutor did not keep a copy of the original document"

-- src:3935 | Original documents to be returned
-- src:3936 | (6) After the accused has received an edited copy of a document, the prosecutor shall keep a copy of the original document, and an edited copy of the document and the original document shall be returned to the packet and the packet resealed.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(6) (src:3935-3936)
GIVEN `the edited copy and the original document have been returned to the packet and the packet resealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has received an edited copy of a document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(6) the edited copy and the original document are returned to the packet and the packet resealed` MEANS
    IF NOT `the accused has received an edited copy of a document`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After the accused has received an edited copy of a document"
    ELSE `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the edited copy and the original document have been returned to the packet and the packet resealed`   -- JUST TRUE when done; JUST FALSE when not yet done ("shall be returned")

-- 187(7): "An accused to whom an edited copy of a document has been provided pursuant to subsection (5) may request that the judge before whom the trial is to be held order that any part of the document deleted by the prosecutor be made available to
-- the accused, and the judge shall order that a copy of any part that, in the opinion of the judge, is required in order for the accused to make full answer and defence and for which the provision of a judicial summary would not be sufficient, be made available to the accused."
-- src:3937 | Deleted parts
-- src:3938 | (7) An accused to whom an edited copy of a document has been provided pursuant to subsection (5) may request that the judge before whom the trial is to be held order that any part of the document deleted by the prosecutor be made available to the accused, and the judge shall order that a copy of any part that, in the opinion of the judge, is required in order for the accused to make full answer and defence and for which the provision of a judicial summary would not be sufficient, be made available to the accused.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(7) (src:3937-3938)
GIVEN `an edited copy of the document has been provided to the accused pursuant to subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made to the judge before whom the trial is to be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(7) the accused may request that the deleted part be made available` MEANS
    IF `an edited copy of the document has been provided to the accused pursuant to subsection (5)` AND `the request is made to the judge before whom the trial is to be held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused to whom an edited copy of a document has been provided pursuant to subsection (5) may request that the judge before whom the trial is to be held"

-- src:3937 | Deleted parts
-- src:3938 | (7) An accused to whom an edited copy of a document has been provided pursuant to subsection (5) may request that the judge before whom the trial is to be held order that any part of the document deleted by the prosecutor be made available to the accused, and the judge shall order that a copy of any part that, in the opinion of the judge, is required in order for the accused to make full answer and defence and for which the provision of a judicial summary would not be sufficient, be made available to the accused.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(7) (src:3937-3938)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the judge the part is required in order for the accused to make full answer and defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the judge the provision of a judicial summary would not be sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(7) the judge shall order that a copy of the part be made available to the accused` MEANS
    IF `in the opinion of the judge the part is required in order for the accused to make full answer and defence` AND `in the opinion of the judge the provision of a judicial summary would not be sufficient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judge shall order that a copy of any part that, in the opinion of the judge, is required in order for the accused to make full answer and defence and for which the provision of a judicial summary would not be sufficient, be made available to the accused"

-- 187(8): "The rules provided for in this section apply to all documents relating to a request for a related warrant or order referred to in subsection 184.2(5), 186(8) or 188(6) with any necessary modifications."
-- src:3939 | Documents to be kept secret — related warrant or order
-- src:3940 | (8) The rules provided for in this section apply to all documents relating to a request for a related warrant or order referred to in subsection 184.2(5), 186(8) or 188(6) with any necessary modifications.
@ref Criminal Code s 187(8) (src:3939-3940)
GIVEN `the documents relate to a request for a related warrant or order referred to in subsection 184.2(5), 186(8) or 188(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 187(8) the rules of the section apply to the documents` MEANS
    IF `the documents relate to a request for a related warrant or order referred to in subsection 184.2(5), 186(8) or 188(6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all documents relating to a request for a related warrant or order referred to in subsection 184.2(5), 186(8) or 188(6)"

§ `Section 189 -- Notice of intention to produce evidence; privileged evidence`

DECLARE `s 189(5) form in which the contents will be adduced` IS ONE OF
    `s 189(5) in the form of a recording`
    `s 189(5) viva voce`
    `s 189(5) in some other form`

-- 189(5): "The contents of a private communication that is obtained from an interception of the private communication pursuant to any provision of, or pursuant to an authorization given under, this Part shall not be received in evidence unless the party
-- intending to adduce it has given to the accused reasonable notice of the intention together with (a) a transcript of the private communication, where it will be adduced in the form of a recording, or a statement setting out full particulars of the private
-- communication, where evidence of the private communication will be given viva voce; and (b) a statement respecting the time, place and date of the private communication and the parties thereto, if known."
-- Named for the bar: JUST TRUE = the contents shall not be received in evidence; JUST FALSE = the "unless" is met (notice with (a) and (b) given); NOTHING = the form of adducing is outside paragraph (a)'s two limbs (not covered).
-- src:3966 | Notice of intention to produce evidence
-- src:3967 | (5) The contents of a private communication that is obtained from an interception of the private communication pursuant to any provision of, or pursuant to an authorization given under, this Part shall not be received in evidence unless the party intending to adduce it has given to the accused reasonable notice of the intention together with
-- src:3968 | (a) a transcript of the private communication, where it will be adduced in the form of a recording, or a statement setting out full particulars of the private communication, where evidence of the private communication will be given viva voce; and
-- src:3969 | (b) a statement respecting the time, place and date of the private communication and the parties thereto, if known.
@ref Criminal Code s 189(5) (src:3966-3969)
GIVEN `the contents are of a private communication obtained from an interception pursuant to any provision of, or pursuant to an authorization given under, this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party intending to adduce it has given the accused reasonable notice of the intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `s 189(5) form in which the contents will be adduced`
      `the notice was given together with a transcript of the private communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given together with a statement setting out full particulars of the private communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given together with a statement respecting the time, place and date of the private communication and the parties thereto, if known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189(5) the contents shall not be received in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contents are of a private communication obtained from an interception pursuant to any provision of, or pursuant to an authorization given under, this Part`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The contents of a private communication that is obtained from an interception of the private communication pursuant to any provision of, or pursuant to an authorization given under, this Part"
        IF NOT `the party intending to adduce it has given the accused reasonable notice of the intention`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the notice was given together with a statement respecting the time, place and date of the private communication and the parties thereto, if known`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF form EQUALS `s 189(5) in the form of a recording`
        THEN IF `the notice was given together with a transcript of the private communication` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be received in evidence unless the party intending to adduce it has given to the accused reasonable notice of the intention together with"
        IF form EQUALS `s 189(5) viva voce`
        THEN IF `the notice was given together with a statement setting out full particulars of the private communication` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be received in evidence unless the party intending to adduce it has given to the accused reasonable notice of the intention together with"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where it will be adduced in the form of a recording, or a statement setting out full particulars of the private communication, where evidence of the private communication will be given viva voce"

-- The notice duty as a regulative rule: "reasonable notice" has no number of days, so no WITHIN.
DECLARE `s 189(5) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 189(5) gives the accused reasonable notice with the transcript or the statement of particulars and the statement of time, place, date and parties`

-- src:3966 | Notice of intention to produce evidence
-- src:3967 | (5) The contents of a private communication that is obtained from an interception of the private communication pursuant to any provision of, or pursuant to an authorization given under, this Part shall not be received in evidence unless the party intending to adduce it has given to the accused reasonable notice of the intention together with
-- src:3968 | (a) a transcript of the private communication, where it will be adduced in the form of a recording, or a statement setting out full particulars of the private communication, where evidence of the private communication will be given viva voce; and
-- src:3969 | (b) a statement respecting the time, place and date of the private communication and the parties thereto, if known.
@ref Criminal Code s 189(5) (src:3966-3969)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 183 party under Part VI` `s 189(5) act`
`s 189(5) the duty to give the accused reasonable notice as a rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 183 the party intending to adduce the intercepted communication`
    MUST `s 189(5) gives the accused reasonable notice with the transcript or the statement of particulars and the statement of time, place, date and parties`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 183 the party intending to adduce the intercepted communication` BECAUSE "s 189(5): the contents were to be adduced without reasonable notice to the accused and the transcript or particulars"

-- 189(6): "Any information obtained by an interception that, but for the interception, would have been privileged remains privileged and inadmissible as evidence without the consent of the person enjoying the privilege."
-- Named for the rule: JUST TRUE = the information remains privileged and inadmissible. With the consent of the person enjoying the privilege the text does not say it is admissible: NOTHING ("without the consent", limited by its own wording).
-- src:3970 | Privileged evidence
-- src:3971 | (6) Any information obtained by an interception that, but for the interception, would have been privileged remains privileged and inadmissible as evidence without the consent of the person enjoying the privilege.
@ref Criminal Code s 189(6) (src:3970-3971)
GIVEN `the information was obtained by an interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for the interception it would have been privileged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enjoying the privilege consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189(6) the information remains privileged and inadmissible as evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the information was obtained by an interception` AND `but for the interception it would have been privileged`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any information obtained by an interception that, but for the interception, would have been privileged"
        IF `the person enjoying the privilege consents`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the person enjoying the privilege"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 190 -- Further particulars`

-- 190: "Where an accused has been given notice pursuant to subsection 189(5), any judge of the court in which the trial of the accused is being or is to be held may at any time order that further particulars be given of the private communication that is intended
-- to be adduced in evidence." A "may ... where" grant: a failed "Where" is JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) (F11); a judge of another court is outside "any judge of the court in which the trial ... is being or is to be held" (NOTHING).
-- src:3972 | Further particulars
-- src:3973 | 190 Where an accused has been given notice pursuant to subsection 189(5), any judge of the court in which the trial of the accused is being or is to be held may at any time order that further particulars be given of the private communication that is intended to be adduced in evidence.
@ref Criminal Code s 190 (src:3972-3973)
GIVEN `an accused has been given notice pursuant to subsection 189(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of the court in which the trial of the accused is being or is to be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 190 the judge may order that further particulars be given of the private communication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an accused has been given notice pursuant to subsection 189(5)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused has been given notice pursuant to subsection 189(5)"
        IF `the person is a judge of the court in which the trial of the accused is being or is to be held`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any judge of the court in which the trial of the accused is being or is to be held"
